1. FORMAL VERIFICATION STRATEGY

We outline the verification pipeline for the composite system.

1. Base protocol.  Carr et al. (2022) have mechanised the safety
   of HotStuff/LibraBFT in Agda; a full liveness proof remains open.
   We assume the base protocol is live under standard BFT assumptions.
2. Safety shield.  The shield σ_s is verified by model‑checking
   its automaton against the safe states of the base protocol.
   Modelling of φ_safety and σ_s in Isabelle/HOL is currently at the
   design stage; a mechanised proof that any action passing σ_s keeps
   the system within the base protocol’s safe region is in progress.
3. Liveness monitor.  The monitor is verified by a simple timeout
   argument: if the agent fails to make progress for k rounds, the
   monitor forces a_safe(s), which the base protocol guarantees
   eventually leads to confirmation.
4. Compositional reasoning.  The addition of the RL agent cannot
   violate safety (all actions are filtered by σ_s) and cannot destroy
   liveness (the monitor periodically takes control).  The formal
   composition proof is planned for the Isabelle/HOL refinement
   framework; LLM‑based proof automation may assist certain sub‑goals.

The present paper reports on the design and on the state of existing
proofs; complete mechanisation remains a long‑term goal.

